  "findings": [
    "Native worker control: missing file leaves hashFiles waiting on unbuffered errs; it does not finish during100ms observation, then terminates once test receives error. Test drains channels and joins worker. Main Generate/Detect statically wait for entries closure before reading errs, creating circular wait on this error path. Full public API timeout not executed.",
    "Parser accepts arbitrary non-SHA256 strings, duplicate hash overwrites original path, unterminated final record accepted; reader errors propagated. All confirmed by actual original helper.",
    "Static Detect trusts catalog digest without reopening catalog reference or final byte comparison; only current candidate Stat checked before optional Remove. No deletion executed.",
    "Static Generate truncates catalog directly; no atomic temporary publication, fsync, close-error propagation or cancellation. Early output failures can abandon producers blocked on channels.",
    "No hard byte/RSS cap: entire catalog map and each directory listing materialized; workers scale with NumCPU; no context cancellation or file-generation guard."
  ],
